Wed Nov  4 04:57:34 AM UTC 2026
$PROBLEM ferx #2656 iiv_on_ruv with a dense R: block_sigma estimation
; Generated by make_data.py. Y = F + F*EXP(ETA(3))*(...): ETA(3) scales every residual SD
; of the subject, so R_i(eta) = exp(2*ETA(3)) * R_i(0).
$INPUT ID TIME DV EVID AMT CMT MDV FREE BLK VIS L2
$DATA pair.csv IGNORE=@
$SUBROUTINES ADVAN1 TRANS2
$PK
  CL = THETA(1)*EXP(ETA(1))
  V  = THETA(2)*EXP(ETA(2))
  S1 = V
$ERROR
  IPRED = F
  RES = (1 - FREE)*EPS(1) + FREE*EPS(2)
  Y = F + F*EXP(ETA(3))*RES
$THETA (0.1, 1.2, 10)
$THETA (1, 12, 100)
$OMEGA 0.1
$OMEGA 0.1
$OMEGA 0.1
$SIGMA BLOCK(2) 0.02 0.005 0.03
$ESTIMATION METHOD=1 INTER MAXEVAL=9999 NSIG=3 SIGL=9 PRINT=5 NOABORT

NM-TRAN MESSAGES
  
 WARNINGS AND ERRORS (IF ANY) FOR PROBLEM    1
             
 (WARNING  2) NM-TRAN INFERS THAT THE DATA ARE POPULATION.
  
Note: Analytical 2nd Derivatives are constructed in FSUBS but are never used.
      You may insert $ABBR DERIV2=NO after the first $PROB to save FSUBS construction and compilation time
  

